          <div class="intro-heading"><p class="intro-affiliation">Computer Science · The University of Hong Kong</p>
          <h1 id="about-title">Hi, I’m Yanlin<span>.</span></h1></div>
          <div class="about-copy">
            <p>I’m currently an MSc student in Computer Science (Financial Computing) at <a href="https://www.hku.hk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the University of Hong Kong</a>.</p>
            <p>My research interests are in <strong>financial AI</strong>, <strong>large language models</strong>, and <strong>reinforcement learning</strong>. My projects so far involve language agents, RL for trading, and alternative data for credit-risk prediction. I’m keen to explore LLMs and RL further, and I’m always happy to chat about research or possible collaborations.</p>
            <p>I previously received a PhD offer from Renmin University of China, and I’m currently looking for PhD opportunities in machine learning and financial AI.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="intro-links"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=PS_CX0AAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/lio-snp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yanlin-liu-1a8882327/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a></div>
